      "message": "Kernel swap: lean runs without swap when no disk is free; reuse only an active swap file\n\nIntegrations notes on 9ea7a5a, Lead 2026-11-12:\n- A split Lean check that finds no disk with 20 GiB free logs \"kernel swap: not enough disk, lean runs\n  without swap\" and runs without swap, as before 9ea7a5a. nanoda keeps the hard error.\n- prepare_kernel_swap reuses bos-kernel.swap only when `swapon --show` lists it. A file that an earlier\n  attempt left before swapon is removed and made again.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
